# tiny-chess engine (make.fun tiny-chess-01, by burns for chase-burns).
# The two lines above are the whole engine in packed form: an lzma-compressed,
# base85-encoded copy of the readable source, unpacked and run at startup.
# Inside: a deterministic alpha-beta engine on a 0x88 board (negamax, fixed
# 40000-node budget, no clock), quiescence, Zobrist TT for move ordering,
# MVV-LVA + killers, hand-tuned arithmetic eval. Size keeps the 4096 cap.
